  m_Name: 5 - Training 5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_training_5
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Multiple Conditions
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Now, we will try to handle situations where the robot must make a
    choice between multiple conditions.


    We will simulate <color=yellow>unstable
    ground</color>, so the environment and minerals will randomize each time you
    press the <color=yellow>Play</color> button. This means every run can produce
    different results, and you cannot rely on a fixed sequence of commands.


    In
    this situation, the robot must check more than one option before deciding what
    to do. You will need to:

    <indent=2em>- Measure both mineral tiles</indent>

    <indent=2em>-
    Compare their values</indent>

    <indent=2em>- Collect the mineral with the
    higher value</indent>


    Please note that different minerals may require different
    handling methods.'
  isImageBig: 0
